mainmenu "bluetooth_rp2_webapp configuration"

comment "Board / platform"

config BOARD_PICO2_W
    bool "Target: Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W (RP2350A)"
    default y
    help
      The validated target. RP2350A, 520 KB SRAM, 4 MB flash, CYW43439
      dual-mode radio. Unset only when building for an RP2040 Pico W, which
      is supported in principle but not validated.

config BOARD_ESP32_C5
    bool "Target: ESP32-C5"
    default n
    depends on !BOARD_PICO2_W
    help
      ESP32-C5, for 5 GHz Wi-Fi. Specified and not built. Pico cmake still
      configures a Pico board. configs/esp32c5_defconfig waits until an
      ESP-IDF build exists. The order is in docs/Feature-Roadmap.md.

